Well as usual, I'm a dolt.
 
The fix is to just add the hosts to each others /etc/hosts file. Thanks
to Oisin for that. Is there somewhere on Tru64 to turn this behaviour
off? 
 
 
Here is the email from Oisin.
 
##############
Two ideas:
i) do you have the ip to name reverse lookup configured for the private
interfaces?
  (Tru64 Unix, on getting a telnet or ftp connection will attempt to
look up the IP address  of the client, and get a name. Setting up names
in /etc/hosts or PTR records in your DNS
  will fix the often considerable timeouts.)
ii) routing: perhaps the server is replying, just over the wrong
interface. Check using traceroute from both ends to make sure both know
the same path over the private network.
 
 
Oisin McGuinness
 
 
Cheers,
Sheldon.




