ORIGINAL MESSAGE:

Hi All,

I know - I should have a backup.... so please don't flame me.

I've blown away my sysconfigtab file on a 5.1A system.

Is there a way to recreate it?


REPLIES FROM AND THANKS TO:

Dan Price
Jason Orendorf
Johan Brusche
Oisin McGuinness


BEST RECOMMENDATIONS:


There is a "template" sysconfigtab (for many other system files
as well) called /etc/.new..sysconfigtab .  Just copy this into
place.  Note that it won't have any customizations or tuning
parameters saved, so you'll need to redo those.


You might be able to use the .proto..sysconfigtab file in /etc 
(use ls -al to see it) as a replacement for sysconfigtab.




Thanks to all!



