---------- Problem Found: Low Voltage Condition - ASC x03 ASCQ x00 at =
Dec 2, 2002 11:40:54 AM GMT+01:00 ----------

Managed Entity:
  Computer Name:        es45 =20
  HS Type:   HSG80  Serial #:       ZG94416851

Service Obligation Data:

   Service Obligation:            Valid
   Service Obligation Number:     invalid
   System Serial Number:          invalid
   Service Provider Company Name: Compaq


Brief Description:
Low Voltage Condition - ASC x03 ASCQ x00

Callout ID:
  FF03000100100107

Severity:
2

Reporting Node:
es45

Full Description:
  This is a drive detected condition that relates to the=20
   o detection of a marginal voltage condition that occurs=20
     at the time the device is in process id writing=20
   o or a servo voltage correction signal that is exceeding=20
     internal drive designed parameters.
 =20
  This is typically NOT a drive issue. This is an environmental=20
  or power problem where insufficient voltage is being supplied=20
  to the drive. It is possible that the enclosure is transmitting=20
  mechanical motion to the drive during heavy seek loads. This=20
  can cause the head/arm assembly to have significant problems=20
  in maintaining tight track following margins that are=20
  inherent on write operations versus read operations.=20
 =20
  Heavy seek activity with multiple drives, or having a tape=20
  drive operating (lots of +12VDC needed to drive the tape=20
  servo) in the same enclosure with low drive input power is=20
  most likely the problem and needs to be=20
  investigated/addressed.=20
 =20
  Drives of Seagate origin, in particular the RZ28M, RZ25L,=20
  RZ29B, and RZ28B have been known to log these events more=20
  often in typical applications.=20
 =20
  Consult Blitz TD 1730A and TD 2130-A for more information.
 =20
                            NOTE:=20
  For FRU codes of 01, 02, 07, 09, 0A and 0B refer to Blitz TD=20
  1730 as these are Input Power Problem related codes.=20
 =20
  For FRU codes of 00 or 11(hex), you might wish to verify or=20
  order and install vibration dampening material that would be=20
  put on an SBB by ordering kit part number 70-32877-01=20
  from Field Service Logistics. This kit contains enough material=20
  to modify 7 SBBs. Refer to Blitz TD 2130A (or later rev).=20
 =20
  The Reported FRU code that is printed in the event log for=20
