For instance:
# grep -E 'tu[0-1]|ee[0-1]' /var/adm/messages | grep selecting | tail -4

Now you just have to decode the speed types. Here are examples of=20
what you might see:

selecting 10Base2 (BNC) port  =3D=3D 10Base2 is BNC (Thin)
selecting 10Base5 (AUI) port  =3D=3D 10Base5 is AUI (Thick)
selecting 10BaseT (UTP) port: half duplex =3D=3D 10BaseT is Twisted-Pair =


>From the console:

P00>>>set ewa0_mode
bad value - valid selections:
        Twisted-Pair
        Full Duplex, Twisted-Pair    <=3D=3D 10BaseT/Twisted-pair
        AUI                          <=3D=3D Thick
        BNC                          <=3D=3D Thin
        Fast
        FastFD (Full Duplex)
        Auto-Negotiate
